w11 (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The input daemon ends itself: when its socket is gone or has been replaced,
    and after fifteen minutes with no client.  A logout that clears the runtime
    directory used to leave one running and unreachable for the rest of the
    uptime, holding the lock that stops the next one starting.
  * wdotool refuses a key combination the active layout cannot produce instead
    of pressing the US position for it, which made ctrl+s on a Greek layout do
    nothing and exit 0.
  * The notice about which layout is assumed reaches every command, not only
    the first, and WDOTOOL_XKB_GROUP is read where the user sets it rather than
    only by a daemon that may already be running.
  * wxrandr --persistent reports a monitors.xml GNOME has already discarded,
    warns when the layout being saved is one a fractional scaling change would
    break, and keeps the previous file beside the new one.
  * A route through GNOME's adjacency rule, behind --unsafe-gnome-overlap, a
    second Shell extension the package now carries, and an agreement recorded
    per libmutter build.  Nothing enables the extension for you.
  * warandr gained the same option in a form that never asks, wxrandr and
    warandr both gained the bookkeeping around it, and neither is handed to the
    real xrandr on an X11 session any more.
  * Everything that differs per GNOME generation is one record in the overlap
    extension's generations.json, which the package now ships, and
    --unsafe-gnome-overlap-unmeasured <major> is the one way past the check
    that this build is one of the measured ones.  GNOME 51 is measured.

 -- Antonio Bianchi <antonio.bianchi.333@gmail.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000

w11 (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: the six tools in /usr/bin, the GNOME Shell bridge
    extension, the /dev/uinput udev rule and the warandr desktop entry, in one
    architecture-independent package that installs on Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04.

 -- Antonio Bianchi <antonio.bianchi.333@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000
